# FastAPI SQLModel

A persistence-first FastAPI starter: SQLModel over an async engine, Alembic
migrations, a generic CRUD base class, and paginated list endpoints.

> Generated project: **<project_name>** — <description>

## When to choose this starter

Pick this template when you want:

- **One model definition per concept.** SQLModel classes are both the
  SQLAlchemy table and the pydantic schema, so a new column is declared once
  in `ItemBase` and every request/response schema inherits it.
- **Async database access all the way down** — `sqlalchemy[asyncio]` engine,
  `AsyncSession` request scope, async Alembic migrations.
- **SQLite for free, PostgreSQL when you need it.** The default
  `DATABASE_URL` is a local SQLite file; point it at
  `postgresql+asyncpg://...` and nothing else changes.
- **CRUD you don't rewrite per domain.** `CRUDBase` supplies create / read /
  list / count / update / delete; each domain subclasses it and adds only
  what is specific to it.

If you don't need a database, start with `fastapi-domain-starter`. If you
want a Docker Compose PostgreSQL stack with synchronous SQLModel, use
`fastapi-psql-orm`.

## Stack

- FastAPI 0.141 / Starlette
- Python 3.12
- SQLModel 0.0.42 on SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async)
- Alembic 1.19
- aiosqlite (default) / asyncpg (optional extra)
- pytest + pytest-asyncio + httpx

## Project structure

```
.
├── README.md
├── pyproject.toml
├── requirements.txt
├── alembic.ini
├── Dockerfile
├── .env
├── .gitignore
├── scripts/
│   ├── format.sh
│   ├── lint.sh
│   ├── migrate.sh          # alembic upgrade head
│   ├── run-server.sh
│   └── test.sh
├── src/
│   └── app/
│       ├── main.py                 # FastAPI app + lifespan
│       ├── core/
│       │   └── config.py           # pydantic-settings configuration
│       ├── db/
│       │   ├── session.py          # async engine, session dependency
│       │   └── base.py             # metadata aggregation for Alembic
│       ├── crud/
│       │   ├── base.py             # generic CRUDBase
│       │   └── pagination.py       # Page[T] envelope
│       ├── alembic/
│       │   ├── env.py              # async migration environment
│       │   └── versions/
│       │       └── 0001_create_items_table.py
│       ├── api/
│       │   ├── router.py           # aggregates health + domain routers
│       │   └── health.py           # GET /health
│       └── domains/
│           └── items/              # example domain
│               ├── models.py       # Item table + Create/Update/Public schemas
│               ├── crud.py         # ItemCRUD(CRUDBase)
│               └── router.py       # FastAPI router
└── tests/
    ├── conftest.py                 # in-memory SQLite fixtures
    ├── test_health.py
    ├── test_items.py
    └── test_crud_base.py
```

## Running the app

```bash
# create a virtualenv and install dependencies
$ uv venv && uv pip install -r requirements.txt
# or: uv sync

# apply migrations
$ bash scripts/migrate.sh

# launch the dev server
$ bash scripts/run-server.sh
# or directly:
$ uvicorn src.app.main:app --reload
```

API docs are then served at:

- Swagger UI: <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs>
- ReDoc:      <http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc>

## API endpoints

| Method | Endpoint                  | Description                          |
|--------|---------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| GET    | `/api/v1/health`          | Liveness probe                       |
| GET    | `/api/v1/items`           | List items (`offset`, `limit`)       |
| GET    | `/api/v1/items/{item_id}` | Read a single item                   |
| POST   | `/api/v1/items`           | Create an item                       |
| PATCH  | `/api/v1/items/{item_id}` | Partially update an item             |
| DELETE | `/api/v1/items/{item_id}` | Delete an item                       |

List responses are wrapped in a page envelope:

```json
{"items": [...], "total": 42, "offset": 0, "limit": 20}
```

## Switching to PostgreSQL

```bash
$ uv pip install "asyncpg>=0.31.0"
$ export DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@localhost:5432/app"
$ bash scripts/migrate.sh
```

`CREATE_TABLES_ON_STARTUP` is convenient against SQLite but should be set to
`false` once Alembic owns the schema.

## Adding a domain

1. Create `src/app/domains/<your_domain>/` mirroring `items`
   (`models.py`, `crud.py`, `router.py`).
2. Import the table model in `src/app/db/base.py` — Alembic autogenerate and
   `create_db_and_tables` only see models that were imported.
3. Register the router in `src/app/api/router.py` (the `# fastkit:imports`
   and `# fastkit:routes` anchors mark where `fastkit addroute` inserts code).
4. Generate a migration: `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add <domain>"`.
5. Add tests under `tests/test_<your_domain>.py`.

## Running tests

```bash
$ bash scripts/test.sh
# or directly:
$ pytest
```

Tests run against a fresh in-memory SQLite database per test — no migrations,
no fixtures files, no cleanup.

## Project Origin

This project was created from the **`fastapi-sqlmodel`** template shipped
with [FastAPI-fastkit](https://github.com/bnbong/FastAPI-fastkit).

The `FastAPI-fastkit` is an open-source project that helps Python and
FastAPI beginners quickly set up a FastAPI-based application development
environment in a framework-like structure.

